    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπαίουχ-ος</span></b>  (properisp.), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>having</i> or <i>gaining trophies</i>:
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεὺς τ.</span> the god <i>to whom
				trophies are dedicated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mu.</u>
				401a23
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				4340
			</span></i><i>f, g</i> (<span class="entity">Pamphylia</span>);
			= Lat. <i>Jupiter Feretrius,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				2.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.306c
			</span></i>; as an epith. of Roman Emperors, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				723.2
			</span></i> (Antinoopolis, <span class="entity">iv A. D.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3992
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Iconium</span>), <i><span class="en">
				4350
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Pamphylia</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				906
			</span></i>
            <u>B</u> (<i><span class="en">
				Magn.
			</span></i> Mae., <span class="entity">iv A. D.</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τροπε-</span>), al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δᾶτις ὁ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Polem.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					41
				</span></i>
			.</div>
